              <a href="/petrol-price-in-kerala/" class="text-sm font-medium text-body hover:text-primary transition-colors">Petrol Price in Kerala</a>
              <a href="/petrol-price-in-haryana/" class="text-sm font-medium text-body hover:text-primary transition-colors">Petrol Price in Haryana</a>
              <a href="/petrol-price-in-odisha/" class="text-sm font-medium text-body hover:text-primary transition-colors">Petrol Price in Odisha</a>
              <a href="/petrol-price-in-india/" class="text-sm font-medium text-body hover:text-primary transition-colors">Petrol Price in India</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="text-body">
            Fuel prices will remain a daily economic indicator for years, even as ethanol blending expands and electric vehicles gain ground. Petrol and diesel still power the overwhelming majority of India's vehicles, and CNG and autogas infrastructure keeps spreading into new cities. Whether you're checking the petrol price in Hyderabad before a fill-up, comparing Rajasthan against Haryana for a road trip, or simply tracking today's rate in your own city, Petrol Price India is built to give you accurate, up-to-date figures in a format that's quick to read and easy to act on.
          </p>
